# Clean codebase

Before finishing any change, leave the touched area **cleaner or no worse** than you found it. Prefer fixing issues you introduce or that sit directly in your path; do not drive-by refactor unrelated modules.

## Remove and avoid

- **Dead code**: unused imports, exports, variables, branches, feature flags, leftover files after moves/deletes, unreachable routes.
- **Duplicates**: copy-paste helpers, parallel types, repeated class strings, twin API clients — extract once to `packages/core` (domain), `apps/api` (persistence/security), or `apps/web` (UI) as appropriate.
- **Comments / TODOs**: follow `no-code-comments.mdc`; do not paper over mess with banners.
- **Speculative abstraction**: no unused generics, config knobs, or “for later” wrappers.

## Performance

- Avoid unnecessary re-renders (unstable inline props/effects only when they already matter in this codebase).
- No N+1 DB work; keep list/query payloads lean (e.g. redact protected map views on public list).
- MapLibre stays client-only; do not pull it into SSR. Prefer existing polling/SSE patterns over new chatty loops.
- Do not add heavy deps when a small local helper suffices.

## Security

- Never weaken passphrase gates, rate limits, CORS allowlist, or header-only `X-Passphrase` (no secrets in URLs/query).
- No logging of passphrases, hashes, or tokens. No committed secrets / `.env` values.
- Validate at boundaries (Zod/UUID params); reject oversized bodies/headers without expensive work when possible.
- Treat authz as server-enforced; UI hiding is not access control.

## Structure

- Domain logic in `packages/core` (no React/Nest). Persistence only in `apps/api`.
- Match Prettier (`prettier-format.mdc`). Run format/typecheck on touched paths before done.
- If behavior/UX/privacy changed, sync docs/site (`docs-and-site-sync.mdc`).

## Done check

Ask: would a reviewer see leftover dead paths, duplicated logic, a perf footgun, or a security shortcut in this diff? If yes, fix it before declaring done.
